# Git branching & pull requests

- Before starting a feature, fix, or non-trivial refactor, create a new branch from the latest default branch.
- Naming:
  - `feature/<short-kebab-name>`
  - `fix/<short-kebab-name>`
  - `chore/<short-kebab-name>`
- Do not commit feature work directly on `main` / `master`.
- Do not force-push shared default branches.
- Keep commits scoped to the branch purpose.
- **When the task is finished**: push the branch (`git push -u origin HEAD`) and open a GitHub pull request into `main` with `gh pr create` (summary + test plan). Use a draft PR if the user still needs to review unfinished work.

```bash
# ✅ GOOD
git checkout -b feature/chat-export
# …implement…
git push -u origin HEAD
gh pr create --title "…" --body "…"

# ❌ BAD
# commit feature changes while still on main
# finish work without opening a PR
```
